WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.330
A small cross on a chain.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.190
Could your employer
tell you to take it off?

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.800
In 2013, Nadia Eweida's case about wearing
her cross at work reached the European

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.790
Court of Human Rights.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.480
Many Muslims point to the Qur'an's words:

6
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.090
there is no compulsion in religion.

7
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.250
So should people be free to show
and share their faith anywhere,

8
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.140
or are there limits?

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.710
In this mission, you'll
explore court cases,

10
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.810
and what the law protects for
people of every belief and none.

11
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.330
Then you'll weigh arguments from believers
and Humanists about whether this freedom

12
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.140
should have any limits.

13
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.940
Your mission: find out whether
faith can be shown anywhere,

14
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.920
and where the limits might fall.
